  "notes": "AutoE2E kitscenes-epoch-5 (the kitscenes_finetune checkpoint of AutowareFoundation/auto_e2e v1.0, auto_e2e pinned at 40a75cf8), driven on Paddock 2eaedb5 (main after #159 and #160) over every route of bench2drive220.xml at Bench2Drive 7ec25d1, the routes set aside for every model left out (issue #158, the 220-route protocol). With upstream's inputs: the measured ego history and the route raster; paddock's camera rig, six cameras. Asked at its declared planning_hz of 10 (one /infer every 0.1 s, the last plan followed in between); early stop at 30 s without 3 m of progress or 4x Think2Drive's time; up to three attempts a route; no site value for anything model.yaml declares; 3 workers on each of two A100 80GB, 7 Nov 06:19 to 8 Nov 09:56 UTC. 1 route(s) set aside for every model (11715: CARLA crashes (signal 11) about 54 s into the route on every attempt, whichever model drives): a route the simulator fails on every time measures no model, so it is in no mean and not counted as lost. 74 of 74 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to autoe2e on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 74/74 source runs recorded. asked for a plan at 10 Hz, the planning_hz the model's model.yaml declared for these runs, the last plan followed in between. early stop (30 s without 3 m of route progress or 4x the expert's time on the route (none on the 9 route(s) here with no expert drive)): a car in a driving scene is expected to move, to finish in reasonable time and not to collide, so a route ended this way is a failed drive, scored as it stood when it ended (a collision's penalty included).",
  "ingested_from": "paddock_runs/bench2drive/autoe2e"
